# Unit 10 单词



## entity
- **音标**: /ˈentəti/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 实体；存在
- **例句**: The company is a separate legal entity.
- **近义词**: being, body, organization
- **派生词**: entities (n. pl.)

## environment
- **音标**: /ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 环境；自然环境
- **例句**: Protecting the environment is everyone's responsibility.
- **近义词**: surroundings, setting, habitat
- **派生词**: environmental (adj.), environmentally (adv.)

## epidemic
- **音标**: /ˌepɪˈdemɪk/
- **词性**: n. adj.
- **释义**: 流行病；流行的
- **例句**: The flu epidemic spread rapidly across the country.
- **近义词**: outbreak, plague, pandemic
- **派生词**: epidemiology (n.)

## episode
- **音标**: /ˈepɪsoʊd/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 一段经历；插曲；（电视）一集
- **例句**: This episode changed his life forever.
- **近义词**: event, incident, installment
- **派生词**: episodic (adj.)

## equal
- **音标**: /ˈiːkwəl/
- **词性**: adj. v. n.
- **释义**: 相等的；平等的；等于
- **例句**: All citizens are equal before the law.
- **近义词**: identical, equivalent, fair
- **派生词**: equality (n.), equally (adv.), unequal (adj.)

## equip
- **音标**: /ɪˈkwɪp/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 装备；配备；使有能力
- **例句**: The school is well equipped with modern technology.
- **近义词**: furnish, supply, provide
- **派生词**: equipment (n.)

## equivalent
- **音标**: /ɪˈkwɪvələnt/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 等同的；对等的人或物
- **例句**: What is the equivalent word in Chinese?
- **近义词**: equal, comparable, corresponding
- **派生词**: equivalence (n.)

## erode
- **音标**: /ɪˈroʊd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 侵蚀；腐蚀；削弱
- **例句**: Wind and rain erode the rocks over time.
- **近义词**: wear away, corrode, deteriorate
- **派生词**: erosion (n.)

## error
- **音标**: /ˈerər/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 错误；过失
- **例句**: There was an error in the calculation.
- **近义词**: mistake, fault, blunder
- **派生词**: erroneous (adj.), err (v.)

## escape
- **音标**: /ɪˈskeɪp/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 逃跑；逃脱；避开
- **例句**: The prisoners escaped from the jail last night.
- **近义词**: flee, run away, avoid
- **派生词**: escapism (n.)

## essay
- **音标**: /ˈeseɪ/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 论文；散文；随笔
- **例句**: She wrote an excellent essay on climate change.
- **近义词**: article, paper, composition
- **派生词**: essayist (n.)

## essential
- **音标**: /ɪˈsenʃl/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 必要的；本质的；要素
- **例句**: Sleep is essential for good health.
- **近义词**: vital, crucial, necessary
- **派生词**: essentially (adv.), essence (n.)

## establish
- **音标**: /ɪˈstæblɪʃ/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 建立；设立；确定
- **例句**: The university was established in 1900.
- **近义词**: found, create, set up
- **派生词**: establishment (n.), established (adj.)

## estimate
- **音标**: /ˈestɪmeɪt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 估计；估算；评价
- **例句**: We estimate the cost at about $10,000.
- **近义词**: assess, calculate, approximate
- **派生词**: estimation (n.), overestimate (v.), underestimate (v.)

## evaluate
- **音标**: /ɪˈvæljueɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 评估；评价
- **例句**: The committee will evaluate all the applications.
- **近义词**: assess, appraise, judge
- **派生词**: evaluation (n.)

## evidence
- **音标**: /ˈevɪdəns/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 证据；证明
- **例句**: There is strong evidence to support the theory.
- **近义词**: proof, testimony, indication
- **派生词**: evident (adj.), evidently (adv.)

## evil
- **音标**: /ˈiːvl/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 邪恶的；罪恶
- **例句**: He is an evil man who has caused much suffering.
- **近义词**: wicked, bad, malevolent
- **派生词**: evilness (n.)

## evolution
- **音标**: /ˌevəˈluːʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 进化；发展；演变
- **例句**: The theory of evolution was proposed by Darwin.
- **近义词**: development, progress, growth
- **派生词**: evolve (v.), evolutionary (adj.)

## exaggerate
- **音标**: /ɪɡˈzædʒəreɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 夸大；夸张
- **例句**: He tends to exaggerate his achievements.
- **近义词**: overstate, amplify, embellish
- **派生词**: exaggeration (n.), exaggerated (adj.)

## examine
- **音标**: /ɪɡˈzæmɪn/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 检查；考试；审查
- **例句**: The doctor examined the patient carefully.
- **近义词**: inspect, test, investigate
- **派生词**: examination (n.), examiner (n.)

## exceed
- **音标**: /ɪkˈsiːd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 超过；超出
- **例句**: The cost exceeded our budget.
- **近义词**: surpass, outdo, go beyond
- **派生词**: exceeding (adj.), exceedingly (adv.), excess (n.), excessive (adj.)

## exception
- **音标**: /ɪkˈsepʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 例外
- **例句**: Everyone must follow the rules without exception.
- **近义词**: anomaly, exclusion
- **派生词**: exceptional (adj.), exceptionally (adv.), except (prep. v.)

## excess
- **音标**: /ɪkˈses/
- **词性**: n. adj.
- **释义**: 过多；过量的
- **例句**: An excess of sugar is bad for your health.
- **近义词**: surplus, extra, too much
- **派生词**: excessive (adj.), excessively (adv.)

## exchange
- **音标**: /ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 交换；交流；兑换
- **例句**: They exchanged gifts at the party.
- **近义词**: swap, trade, barter
- **派生词**: exchangeable (adj.)

## exclude
- **音标**: /ɪkˈskluːd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 排除；排斥；不包括
- **例句**: The price excludes tax and delivery charges.
- **近义词**: bar, omit, reject
- **派生词**: exclusion (n.), exclusive (adj.), exclusively (adv.)

## execute
- **音标**: /ˈeksɪkjuːt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 执行；处决；实施
- **例句**: The plan was executed perfectly.
- **近义词**: carry out, implement, perform
- **派生词**: execution (n.), executive (n. adj.)

## exempt
- **音标**: /ɪɡˈzempt/
- **词性**: adj. v.
- **释义**: 被免除的；豁免
- **例句**: Students are exempt from paying the tax.
- **近义词**: excused, excluded, free
- **派生词**: exemption (n.)

## exert
- **音标**: /ɪɡˈzɜːrt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 施加；运用；努力
- **例句**: He exerted great influence on the decision.
- **近义词**: apply, exercise, use
- **派生词**: exertion (n.)

## exhaust
- **音标**: /ɪɡˈzɔːst/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 使筋疲力尽；用尽；排气
- **例句**: The long hike exhausted everyone.
- **近义词**: tire, deplete, drain
- **派生词**: exhaustion (n.), exhausting (adj.), exhausted (adj.)

## exhibit
- **音标**: /ɪɡˈzɪbɪt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 展览；展示；表现
- **例句**: The museum exhibits ancient artifacts.
- **近义词**: display, show, demonstrate
- **派生词**: exhibition (n.), exhibitor (n.)

## expand
- **音标**: /ɪkˈspænd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 扩大；扩展；膨胀
- **例句**: The company plans to expand its business overseas.
- **近义词**: enlarge, extend, grow
- **派生词**: expansion (n.), expansive (adj.)

## exploit
- **音标**: /ɪkˈsplɔɪt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 开发；利用；剥削
- **例句**: We should exploit renewable energy sources.
- **近义词**: utilize, take advantage of, abuse
- **派生词**: exploitation (n.), exploitable (adj.)

## explore
- **音标**: /ɪkˈsplɔːr/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 探索；探险；研究
- **例句**: The scientists explored the depths of the ocean.
- **近义词**: investigate, examine, discover
- **派生词**: exploration (n.), explorer (n.)

## expose
- **音标**: /ɪkˈspoʊz/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 暴露；揭露；使接触
- **例句**: The journalist exposed the corruption scandal.
- **近义词**: reveal, uncover, disclose
- **派生词**: exposure (n.), exposition (n.)

## extend
- **音标**: /ɪkˈstend/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 延伸；扩展；提供
- **例句**: The deadline has been extended by two weeks.
- **近义词**: stretch, expand, prolong
- **派生词**: extension (n.), extensive (adj.), extensively (adv.)

## external
- **音标**: /ɪkˈstɜːrnl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 外部的；外面的
- **例句**: The external walls of the building need painting.
- **近义词**: outer, outside, exterior
- **派生词**: externally (adv.), internal (反义)

## extract
- **音标**: /ɪkˈstrækt/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 提取；摘录；榨取
- **例句**: They extracted oil from the ground.
- **近义词**: remove, withdraw, derive
- **派生词**: extraction (n.)

## extreme
- **音标**: /ɪkˈstriːm/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 极端的；极度的；极端
- **例句**: The region experiences extreme weather conditions.
- **近义词**: intense, severe, utmost
- **派生词**: extremely (adv.), extremism (n.), extremist (n.)
